            <div xml:id="d592">

                <pb facs="0626" n="526" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg526"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/7512: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Macgowan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-12T16:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">October 12,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 12—11:57
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>53. Fifteen thousand refugees from Habarovsk arrived here.</p>
                <p>Robberies, murders increasing Vladivostok and inhabitants. Swedish consul’s
                    country home plundered daylight, himself and family menaced. Consular corps
                    probably will be asked to renew request to Japan to protect foreigners which was
                    made by them when Caldwell was robbed. This request was based on responsibility
                    assumed by the Japanese when they disarmed Maritime Provinces military forces.
                    Without authority from the Department I cannot join in such request; please
                    instruct. It has been informally suggested that the Allied Powers should return
                    sufficient contingents to establish international police as the local
                    authorities are powerless and are facing speedy bankruptcy. I offer no
                    opinion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Macgowan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
